{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Among the elim</b> — two times in the Masorah: מי כמוכה באלים / הנחמים באלים. They interpreted it concerning idolatry: that they make it beneath trees, like beneath the elah, and they are accustomed to make an asherah that has shade, for there are asherot that have fruit but have no shade, and these have shade but have no fruit. But the Holy One, blessed be He — His shade is beautiful and His fruits are sweet, and He has shade. And this is what is written: בצלו חמדתי וישבתי ופריו מתוק לחכי."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The two Masorah citations are from Exodus 15:11 and Psalms 31:7 respectively; the final citation is from Song of Songs 2:3. The second Masorah quotation reads הנחמים in the source but the Psalms verse reads הנחנים; preserved exactly as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:04.040545375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}